// Two allocations in different threads, which no program order relates.
// Thread 1 frees rp, and nothing orders thread 2's malloc before that free,
// so rq may be rp's region handed back out: the allocator, not the program,
// orders the free before the reuse (C11 7.22.3p2; #225). Until the free map
// this was forbidden, for want of a free happening before the malloc (R17,
// #103).
{
  rp := malloc 1;
  free(rp);
} ||| {
  rq := malloc 1;
}
%%
allow (rp = rq) []
